{
  "summary": "Restricts sighash verification in `SignPSBTInput` to run only when an explicit sighash type option or `PSBT_IN_SIGHASH_TYPE` is specified, permitting existing signatures to use any sighash type when unspecified. Additionally, updates `RemoveUnnecessaryTransactions` to inspect Taproot signatures and final witness elements for `SIGHASH_ANYONECANPAY` before pruning `non_witness_utxo` data.",
  "problem": "`SignPSBTInput` enforced assumed default sighash types (`SIGHASH_DEFAULT` for Taproot, `SIGHASH_ALL` for legacy/segwit) even when no sighash type was provided, causing valid PSBTs with differing signature sighashes (such as 65-byte Taproot signatures) to fail validation with `SIGHASH_MISMATCH` and preventing subsequent signing or finalization. Concurrently, `RemoveUnnecessaryTransactions` relied solely on the `PSBT_IN_SIGHASH_TYPE` field to detect `SIGHASH_ANYONECANPAY`, leading to inappropriate deletion of `non_witness_utxo` entries when the field was absent or stripped during finalization.",
  "evidence": [
    "Issue #36507 reports that `SignPSBTInput rejects valid 65-byte taproot script signatures when PSBT_IN_SIGHASH_TYPE is absent`.",
    "PR description: 'A PSBT holding a valid 65-byte SIGHASH_ALL taproot signature could then be neither finalized nor signed further.'"
  ],
