  "changed_since_previous": "The PR now completely skips existing signature sighash checks when no sighash type is provided (rather than only allowing 65-byte Taproot signatures with SIGHASH_ALL). It also adds inspection of Taproot signatures and finalized witness stacks in `RemoveUnnecessaryTransactions` to preserve `non_witness_utxo` data for `SIGHASH_ANYONECANPAY`.",
  "card": "Restricts sighash checks in SignPSBTInput to only run when an explicit sighash type or PSBT_IN_SIGHASH_TYPE field is present, conforming to BIP 174 by allowing signers to use arbitrary sighash types when unconstrained. Previously, omitting the sighash type caused SignPSBTInput to assume defaults and reject valid non-default signatures (such as 65-byte Taproot signatures), blocking further signing or finalization. The PR also ensures RemoveUnnecessaryTransactions inspects Taproot and final witness signatures for SIGHASH_ANYONECANPAY so required non-witness UTXOs are preserved. This addresses issue #36507.",
